 "premise": "Umiko Chino, a 65-year-old widow, goes to the cinema for the first time in years and meets Kai, a film student who, like her, watches the audience more than the screen. Kai challenges her to pursue her own wish to make films, and she enrolls at his art school. There she struggles to understand a much younger generation's ambitions while finding her own voice through filmmaking.",
 "life_message": "It is never too late to pursue what you truly want to make, and creative work connects people across generations.",
